# ACE single-point LAMMPS/pair_style-pace evaluation -- analogous to the
# VASP_ReaxFF_LAMMPs example's own in.single_point, but for ACE instead of
# ReaxFF: units metal (CONFIRMED required -- pair_pace.cpp itself rejects
# any other units directive, "ACE potentials require 'metal' units"),
# atom_style atomic (no charges/qeq fix -- ACE has no charge-equilibration
# step at all, unlike ReaxFF), no cell minimization (`run 0` evaluates the
# structure exactly as read, matching pyace's own PyACECalculator never
# relaxing before get_potential_energy()/get_forces(), so FF-vs-reference
# comparisons stay apples-to-apples).
#
# Deliberately does NOT use the /kk Kokkos-suffixed pair_style directly --
# lammps_ace_single_point.py activates Kokkos via LAMMPS's own `-sf kk`
# command-line suffix instead (auto-appends /kk to pair_style/etc.), so this
# same .in file works for both the Kokkos-GPU chore this was written for and
# a plain-CPU run (e.g. for local debugging) without editing it.
#
# `pace product` (not bare `pace`, and not `pace recursive`) -- CONFIRMED
# (2026-10-13) via a real GPU allocation: pair_pace_kokkos.cpp's own
# coeff()/compute() REQUIRES the product algorithm on the GPU ("Must use
# 'product' algorithm with pair pace/kk on the GPU") and errors otherwise --
# this was missed in the original smoke test, which only ever exercised
# plain CPU `pair_style pace` (no GPU available on the login node to catch
# this). `product` is also valid on CPU (LAMMPS's own
# examples/PACKAGES/pace/in.pace.product), so this one spelling works for
# both Kokkos-GPU and plain-CPU runs without a conditional.
#
# Variables (ff_filename, structure, elements) are set by
# lammps_ace_single_point.py via `lmp.command("variable ... string ...")`
# before this file is loaded via `lmp.file(...)`.

units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style atomic
box tilt large
processors * * *
newton on
neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

read_data ${structure}

pair_style pace product
pair_coeff * * ${ff_filename} ${elements}

thermo 1
thermo_style custom step temp pe epair etotal press pxx pyy pzz lx ly lz vol density

run 0
